# Files auto-copied into a new `git worktree` created via `claude --worktree`
# (gitignore syntax). These are gitignored files a fresh worktree lacks but needs.
# Newer Claude Code honors this file natively on WorktreeCreate; the cold path is
# scripts/new-worktree.sh, which copies the SAME set explicitly (:95) — keep the
# two in step, because only new-worktree.sh runs on the handoff-fire and
# cc-dispatch lanes, which do not go through WorktreeCreate.
#
# Why this repo needs it at all: `.claude/settings.local.json` holds the
# per-worktree permission grants. Absent, every fresh worktree re-prompts for
# commands the operator already approved — and a worktree is created per session
# here, so the cost is paid constantly. It must be COPIED, never symlinked:
# a symlink would make every worktree mutate the shared file, which is the same
# shared-state defect worktree isolation exists to prevent (new-worktree.sh:93).
#
# Absent from this repo until 2026-09-19 while six sibling repos on this machine
# carried one (doc_classifier, reso-management-app, reso-management-app-release,
# reso-qa-runner, dc-corpus, dc-wiring).
.claude/settings.local.json
.env
.env.local
